course: dictionary
lesson: 1571
title: Charger: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. «Use the right charger, and stop charging if a phone or battery gets hot.» The clues phone and battery tell you that a charger here is a device that puts electricity back into a battery.
explain: Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence. Things are being charged and plugged in, so a charger must be a cable or plug. Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense: "Use the right device that puts electricity into a battery" works.
explain: The dictionary also lists two less common meanings: a horse ridden by a knight in old stories, and a large flat plate. Look for clues such as knight, battle or dinner before choosing one of these. If the words around it talk about phones and batteries, the everyday meaning is almost always right.
fact: Charger means a device that puts electricity back into a battery, like a phone or laptop charger.
fact: In old stories, a charger is a horse ridden by a knight into battle.
fact: A charger can also mean a large flat plate, but this meaning is rare.
fact: «Under a pillow or duvet the heat cannot escape», so never charge a phone on your bed.
fact: Good clue words for the device meaning include battery, phone, plug and cable.
exercise: «Use the right charger, and stop charging if a phone or battery gets hot.» What is a charger in this sentence? | *A device that puts electricity back into a battery | A toy car | A horse ridden into battle | A large flat plate
exercise: In an old story, a knight rode into battle on a powerful horse called a what? | *charger | plug | plate | cable
exercise: Which is a safe place to charge your phone? | *On a hard surface with a proper charger | Under a pillow | Under the duvet | On the bed next to the cushions
test: «A fast charger can add a lot of range in about twenty to thirty minutes.» What does charger mean here? | A bedtime story | A horse for a knight | A flat plate for food | *A device that puts electricity into a car's battery
test: Which words are the best clues that charger means a device here? | knight and battle | horse and stable | *battery and phone | plate and dinner
exam: In «Cheap fake chargers may skip safety parts, get very hot and start fires», what does charger mean? | A horse for a knight | A flat plate for food | *A device that puts electricity into a battery | A cook's dish
